  "selected": [
    {
      "id": "cmip6-mlotst-definition",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-mlotst-definition.md",
      "sha256": "7c9f821afb300a640b26dbd03993d309a09793518640191dc82d641f6a4f5cb5",
      "reason": "Defines the surface-referenced sigma-t criterion (Δρ ≈ 0.03 kg m-3, evaluated at local pressure) that the operator MLD must reproduce, and says mlotst is computed online every time step.",
      "notes_cut": 2,
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Compute the operator MLD with `compute_mixed_layer_depth` using 0.03 kg m-3 (ΔB_crit = 0.0003 m s-2) and `ref_depth` equal to each model's shallowest level, not the 10 m default. `mlotst` is referenced to the ocean surface. Compute the MLD of each monthly profile first, then average the MLDs over the 30 Marches or Septembers. Never average T and S first.",
        "Exclude columns where the offline operator finds no crossing, and report how much area that removes. Models encode these columns differently. GFDL-ESM4 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR give roughly the full column depth, and CESM2 gives 0 m in many Arctic-shelf cells. Do not use a single fill value."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "monthly-means-are-time-averages",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "pitfalls/monthly-means-are-time-averages.md",
      "sha256": "df6b5c23460f88f1522e5c6a665e1efbb8322c3ae876c885530f3019aa284ee0",
      "reason": "The operator MLD is computed offline from monthly-mean thetao and so, a nonlinear diagnostic that differs from the online mlotst, which is the main reason they are not expected to agree exactly.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "The operator MLD is a diagnostic of averaged states, whereas `mlotst` is the time mean of instantaneous diagnostics. Nonlinear f(monthly mean) ≠ monthly mean of f, so say which order was used.",
        "Do not use `compute_basic_stat(op='mean')` for period means because it weights months equally. Here each calendar month is averaged across the 30 years, which is a plain mean of that month's values and needs no day weights. A monthly climatology is a plain mean over years."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "Bias, RMSE and correlation exist only where both fields have data, so each model and month needs one mask covering both fields in all 30 instances.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Build the comparison mask where both fields are valid in all 30 instances of that month, using `build_comparison_mask`. Apply it to both fields with `.where(mask)` before any metric. Use `ocean_only=False`, since no WOA23 is involved.",
        "Report the `mean_data`/`mean_reference` and bias from `compute_difference_metrics` over the shared sample. Report the mask cell counts and area, and the share of total ocean area covered. A small mask means the products disagree about where data are defined."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "missing-values-and-land-cells",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "pitfalls/missing-values-and-land-cells.md",
      "sha256": "f576244f13dde06fed1777eaa9721c68844f61758f66fac704b44f1551e90df2",
      "reason": "Land and below-sea-floor cells carry the 1e20 missing value, which would dominate the means, RMSE and area percentages if the CF masking is skipped.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Build each field's valid mask from the field itself, because `thetao`, `so` and `mlotst` masks can differ within a model. Use NaN-aware reductions with weights masked to the same cells. A value near 1e20 in an output is an unmasked fill value.",
        "Use `compute_exceedance_fraction` for the share of area with |difference| > 20 m. It leaves missing cells out of the numerator and denominator, and returns the area in m2."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "The mean difference, RMSE and area percentages must be area-weighted with areacello, with no subsampling.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Weight the mean difference and RMSE by each model's own `areacello` on the shared mask: use `compute_difference_metrics`, which weights by area by default. Use `analyze_correlation` with `weighting='area'` for the spatial Pearson correlation.",
        "The >20 m percentage is a share of area, not of cells, and its denominator is the area where both fields are defined. Give the coverage as a percentage of the model's total ocean area."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-grid-labels",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "datasets/cmip6-grid-labels.md",
      "sha256": "e349f9e305621b6c10b35cccd0490da521cc7e3ba08bfb53890479f81024d117",
      "reason": "GFDL-ESM4 is on a regridded gr grid while CESM2 and MPI are native gn, which affects the masks, the operator MLD's exactness and the ocean-area fractions.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "GFDL-ESM4 is on a regridded 1° archive grid (`gr`), while CESM2 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR are on `gn`. Each model is compared on its own grid with its own `areacello`. Regrid to lon-lat only for display in the figures, not for the metrics."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-thetao-potential-temperature",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-thetao-potential-temperature.md",
      "sha256": "cf8b1424a04be2e18362300d2e76d09e3f958f9d6a451c733a0cf9938968e73c",
      "reason": "thetao is potential temperature referenced to 0 dbar, so the density for the criterion needs the correct treatment of potential temperature versus in-situ pressure.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`thetao` is potential temperature, and no local model provides `bigthetao`. Use the potential-temperature route for the density calculation (see `temperature_kind()`), not the in-situ route."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-so-practical-salinity",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-so-practical-salinity.md",
      "sha256": "96f2763290996040d675ca6e8f997ea29fa320b8f6e6793bf2c6fcb739345e19",
      "reason": "so is Practical Salinity, and the density calculation (for example with TEOS-10) needs Absolute Salinity derived from it.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`so` is Practical Salinity (units \"0.001\") with values of order 35, so do not rescale it. For TEOS-10 density, convert S_P to S_A before calling gsw routines that expect S_A."
      ]
    }
